{% extends 'shells/docs.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Documentation · php-via{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<article>
    <h1>Documentation</h1>
    <p>
        Welcome to the php-via docs. Pick a path below depending on where you're starting from.
    </p>

    <h2>New to php-via?</h2>
    <p>Start with the tutorial. It walks you through building a reactive counter from scratch and introduces all three core primitives (signals, actions, views).</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/getting-started" class="btn btn-primary" style="display: inline-flex;">Getting Started →</a></p>

    <h2>Upgrading from 0.13?</h2>
    <p><a href="/docs/upgrading">Upgrading to 0.14</a> takes a 0.13 app to 0.14 in the order the errors appear, with a worked example.</p>

    <h2>Understand the concepts</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/signals">Signals</a>: reactive state and how it binds to the DOM</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/actions">Actions</a>: server-side event handlers</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/views">Views</a>: what a tab shows, how it updates and when tabs share a render</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/scopes">Scopes</a>: TAB, ROUTE, SESSION, GLOBAL, and custom</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/components">Components</a>: isolated sub-contexts for composable UI</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/composition">Composition</a>: class-based pages and components with PHP attributes</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/broadcasting">Broadcasting</a>: pushing updates to groups of clients</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/lifecycle">Lifecycle</a>: connect, disconnect, revival, timers and cleanup</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Guides</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/middleware">Middleware</a>: PSR-15 middleware, auth, plain routes, security</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/twig">Templates</a>: shells, the page bootstrap, Twig and other engines, CSP</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/web-components">Web components</a>: Rocket and Starbase components on php-via pages</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/dev-bar">Dev Bar</a>: traces, signals, patches and logs in the page</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/development">Development</a>: the dev server, hot reload and tests</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/deployment">Deployment with OpenSwoole and Caddy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/broker">Multi-node broker</a>: broadcasts across workers and servers</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/performance">Performance</a>: what a page view, a tab, an action and a broadcast cost, and how many fit on a server</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/design">Design decisions</a>: why persistent SSE, server-side state, and declarative scopes</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reference</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/api">API reference</a>: every public method with its signature</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/comparisons">Comparison with other frameworks</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/faq">Common pitfalls</a>: bugs that are easy to hit and hard to diagnose</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/mbolli/php-via/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Changelog ↗</a></li>
    </ul>
</article>

{% endblock %}
